{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1072053-how-far-away-can-i-see-smell-feel-it","id":1072053,"title":"How far away can I see / smell / feel it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-02T09:34:39-07:00","id":1072053,"title":"How far away can I see / smell / feel it?","content":"Questions about sensory effects that we've realized we're not sure about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> From how far away will active effects ping my peripheral mage sight?<br /> How far does my active mage sight reach? As far as normal sight (or scent or smell or whatever sense is used to experience Mage &quot;sight&quot;)?<br /> <br /> And regarding specific sensory spells?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sacred Geometry implies that casting the spell just grants your otherwise normal senses the ability to detect ley lines and nodes (that is, it extends detection to sensory range).<br /> <br /> Exorcist's Eye doesn't specify how far away you can detect spirits.<br /> <br /> Speak to the Dead, and Detect Substance say the applicable spell lets you see / detect said thing within area of affect. This means if you have one dot in the arcanum and don't want to spend extra reach (or are designing this as an instant level one attainment for a legacy), you will see ghosts / sterling silver etc. if it is standing within about two and a half feet of you. Not useless, but it involves very tedious searching.<br /> <br /> Considering 2nd Ed. strives for consistency between arcana, I'm hoping I'm missing something here. How do you run these spells?<br /> <br /> If this actually is clarified in the book and I missed it, or already discussed on the forum and my search failed, please if possible just give me the page number or link to the discussions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T16:46:08-07:00","id":1072245,"title":"","content":"I run it like this:<br /> <br /> For Knowing spells, subjects have to be within your spell's range. So increasing Scale to encompass multiple subjects won't be much worth if your basic range is touch range, unless you touch multiple subjects. <br /> <br /> Unlike Knowing spells, Unveiling spells grant expanded sensory abilities to the subject. So you could cast Speak With the Dead on a friend across the street (in sensory range and within the spell's Scale) and then he'd be able to see ghosts within his own sensory range, which may well be outside your spell's Scale. <br /> <br /> Hope that made sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T17:35:54-07:00","id":1072262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1072053-how-far-away-can-i-see-smell-feel-it?p=1072245#post1072245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I run it like this:<br /> <br /> For Knowing spells, subjects have to be within your spell's range. So increasing Scale to encompass multiple subjects won't be much worth if your basic range is touch range, unless you touch multiple subjects.<br /> <br /> Unlike Knowing spells, Unveiling spells grant expanded sensory abilities to the subject. So you could cast Speak With the Dead on a friend across the street (in sensory range and within the spell's Scale) and then he'd be able to see ghosts within his own sensory range, which may well be outside your spell's Scale.<br /> <br /> Hope that made sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does make sense.<br /> <br /> I was thinking just in terms of divinatory magic in general, and it didn't occur to me to look specifically to the practices the game makers spelled out so clearly. If I had I would have seen that the description for unveiling effects does say that they reveal things &quot;to the mage's senses&quot;, which would imply it grants the perception to your sensory range (it even refers to seeing things &quot;across a landscape&quot;).<br /> <br /> The only sticking point for me is that the description for &quot;speak to the dead&quot; spells out that you can see ghosts &quot;within the area of affect&quot;. This may just be an error in the manual, but after the time it took to create 2nd ed., and then again to gather info. and release the final copy, my impression is that there are very few if any actual errors in the rule book. This makes me think I am missing something.<br /> <br /> But I will not worry about it and will run things as you do unless given another reason to do otherwise. Thanks for the response!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T17:48:36-07:00","id":1072268,"title":"","content":"Thanks in turn. Good huntings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T23:29:49-07:00","id":1072379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1072053-how-far-away-can-i-see-smell-feel-it?p=1072245#post1072245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I run it like this:<br /> <br /> For Knowing spells, subjects have to be within your spell's range. So increasing Scale to encompass multiple subjects won't be much worth if your basic range is touch range, unless you touch multiple subjects.<br /> <br /> Unlike Knowing spells, Unveiling spells grant expanded sensory abilities to the subject. So you could cast Speak With the Dead on a friend across the street (in sensory range and within the spell's Scale) and then he'd be able to see ghosts within his own sensory range, which may well be outside your spell's Scale.<br /> <br /> Hope that made sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you cast a spell via sensory range on a subject on the other side of the street you increase the scale of the spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T02:14:19-07:00","id":1072414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1072053-how-far-away-can-i-see-smell-feel-it?p=1072379#post1072379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you cast a spell via sensory range on a subject on the other side of the street you increase the scale of the spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Range and Scale are removed. What I meant was that Unveiling spells work by granting sensory abilities to the subject, so the subject has to be within both range and Scale. But what the subject perceives with his newfound senses after the spell was cast can be outside the spell's range and Scale. Knowing spells, on the other hand, work 'normally' by delivering information about the subject to the mage, so the subject has to stay within range and Scale.<br /> <br /> It works like this:<br /> 1) You try to cast an Unveiling spell (eg. Speak With the Dead), which grants new sensory capabilities to the subject (in this case, sensing of ghosts), on your Sleepwalker retainer across the street. Because the spell's subject is not within touch range, you cast at sensory range. Because you're targeting only that one Sleepwalker, the spell's Scale factor is left at 1.<br /> 2) You change your mind and decide to send a group of Sleepwalker retainers across the street. The spell is still cast at sensory range. Now, because you're targeting a bunch of people, you increase the Scale factor by a few steps.<br /> 3) The Sleepwalkers come back and debrief you on what they saw. Oh, and they brought a corpse to you for investigation. You cast a Knowing spell (Forensic Gaze, in this case), which delivers information about its subject straight to the caster (in this case, the cause and time of death of a corpse). The subject (corpse) is right in front of you, so you just cast the spell at touch range. You also only have a single subject (one corpse), so you put the spell's Scale factor at 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T03:39:33-07:00","id":1072430,"title":"","content":"Got it. I just thought: &quot;how can a single subject ever be out of scale of a spell?&quot;, but you were just including the possibility of multiple subjects in that frasing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T03:40:48-07:00","id":1072431,"title":"","content":"You also have to account for Size unless you're casting AoE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T03:57:58-07:00","id":1072437,"title":"","content":"But only when the Size exceeds 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}